        <div class="content">
          <div class="article">
            <h1><strong>How can I help you?</strong></h1>
            <p style="max-width: 983px;">Greetings, and welcome to KnowsMore!
              Please use the search bar on the home page. Well, I’d be happy to
              provide recommendations for your queries at any time, upon
              request! (As long as you are polite…)</p>
            <hr class="divider">
            <h2><strong>General</strong></h2>
            <details>
              <summary>What is KnowsMore?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">KnowsMore is a search engine that
                allows users to search for information within the digital realm.
                It pays homage to older search engines like Ask Jeeves!</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What makes KnowsMore different from other search engines?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">Back in the early 2000s, Ask Jeeves
                was ahead of his time. People formatted their queries in natural
                language to get search results. Inspired by Ask Jeeves,
                KnowsMore uses AI to process natural language and provide search
                results in different languages, such as Spanish, Chinese,
                French, and many more!</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What does KnowsMore stand for?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">KnowsMore is the combination of two
                words, Knows and More. “Knows” means to have information. “More”
                emphasizes the “Knows” in knowledge to a greater extent. This
                word choice combination creates KnowsMore, which develops the
                pursuit of knowledge.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What is that little graduate/professor mascot?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">That is Mr. KnowsMore, the mascot for
                the KnowsMore search engine! Think of him as the embodiment of
                this very site.</p>
            </details>
            <hr class="divider">
            <h2><strong>Browse the Web</strong></h2>
            <details>
              <summary>What can I search for?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">You can search for any information
                available on the internet! Feel free to search for events, jobs,
                hotels, information, etc from the comfort of your device.
                Remember to keep your queries appropriate for a professional
                setting.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How can I make a search query?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">Think of Ask Jeeves. You can search
                by keyword or use natural language to pose questions to
                KnowsMore, who does his very best to answer them. To get the
                best results, you can format your queries into questions.</p>
            </details>
            <hr class="divider">
            <h2><strong>Data and Information Confidentiality</strong></h2>
            <details>
              <summary>How does KnowsMore use my data and information?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">KnowsMore respects the privacy of all
                users. KnowsMore only keeps track of your search history. When
                you create queries, KnowsMore makes personalized recommendations
                based on past search predictions. KnowsMore only keeps your
                information confidential and uses it to enhance the relevancy of
                the search results. Any collected data remains confidential.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can I clear my search history?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">Yes, you can clear your search
                history. Enable incognito mode on your browser or delete all
                cookies.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Is my data shared with third parties?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">No, your data is kept confidential.
                KnowsMore does not sell your data to third parties.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Do I need an account to use KnowsMore?</summary>
              <p style="max-width: 983px;">No, you do not need an account.
                KnowsMore is free to use!</p>
            </details>
            <hr class="divider">
